Desperately trying to break away, you attempt to take hand-made machete out of the bag, but dreadful branches surround you from all sides, and each new movement is getting harder to make. Soon arms and legs are tightly adhered. 
Spots of skin uncovered by clothing begin to burn. At first a little, but then burning pain becomes intolerable. The wind muffles weak cry for help, and soon your body hangs upon the predatory branches, that greedily drain your life. Your adventure ends here.